Q: Platform-independent way to get the user&#39;s home directory in C++ A: <p>Well you simply can't do that : &lt;pwd.h&gt; is for UNIX systems, but what you can use : filesystem combined with preprocessor directives, here is a code sample :<br />
`</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;
#include &lt;cstdlib&gt; // for std::getenv
#include &lt;filesystem&gt; // for std::filesystem

std::filesystem::path get_home_dir() {
    const char* homeDir = nullptr;
#if defined(_WIN32)
    homeDir = std::getenv(&quot;USERPROFILE&quot;);
#else 
    homeDir = std::getenv(&quot;HOME&quot;);
#endif
    if (homeDir) return std::filesystem::path(homeDir);

    // return an empty path if nothing is found
    return std::filesystem::path();
}
</code></pre>
<p>`</p>
